From 98ec3bdca457f3ef10a099cbd2709ccbfa0ffde1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@ubuntu.localdomain>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:42:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(rlharness): v4.0.0 harness skeleton with working
 control protocol

Adds the TH08_RL_HARNESS build option (default OFF) and the first vertical
slice of the v4.0.0 training ground (10-P0 WP3):

- src/rlharness/rlharness.hpp / .cpp: line-oriented control protocol over a
  pipe pair (HELLO, PING, FRAME, HASH, STATE, STEP, QUIT), plus state export of
  the 25 tracked fields and a FNV-1a 64 state hash.
- src/main.cpp: GameWindow::Render()'s body without the timing gate becomes
  PumpOneFrame(), and WinMain enters rlharness::Run() instead of the message
  loop when --rl-control is present.
- src/Global.cpp: Controller::GetInput() returns the commanded mask, so input
  still flows through RecordInputAndFps and keeps the real +1 frame latency.
- CMake: option(TH08_RL_HARNESS OFF); when ON it also defines
  TH08_ENABLE_REPLAY_TRACE because Rng::ReplayTraceGenerationCount() is field 15
  of the tracked set and lives behind that guard.

The 25 tracked fields are copied verbatim from replay_trace.cpp, the field set
already proven bit-identical against the retail replay corpus.

Argument parsing reads /proc/self/cmdline: linux_runtime.cpp keeps argv in an
anonymous namespace, so another TU cannot reach it without touching the
platform layer.

Verified: builds clean, passes scripts/verify-portable-linux.sh, and a smoke
test drives HELLO/STEP/HASH/STATE/QUIT end to end (120 frames advance under
command control, hashes change with state, RNG seed visible in the export).

Not yet implemented: RESET/StageStart, pixel readback, shared memory, shadow
role, BRANCH/PARK/SPAWN, null-device mode.
